5	    A method whose one parameter is a tuple compiles: its JVM parameters follow its declaration, and bridges join a boxed tuple to a body's elements
6	    
7	    Climb batch 31b, rung T (rows 992, 832, 819, 397 and 840). The code
8	    generator passes a parameter of a declared tuple type as the tuple's
9	    elements, and a generic trait's method over a type parameter takes one
10	    boxed tuple at a tuple instance, so an object's body written at the tuple
11	    type did not implement it and its class failed verification: every
12	    m[i,j] of the one library's arrays of rank 2 and 3. Now a bridge of the
13	    boxed signature calls the body with the elements, the class loader's
14	    twin is made only where a tuple is substituted in, a dotted call passes
15	    the tuple boxed where the receiver's declarations take it so, the
16	    forwarders count JVM parameters, and an operator on one tuple operand
17	    passes its elements. Row 237 is noted, and rows 1054 to 1057 are new: an
18	    overloaded method at a pair, an object's one pair value parameter, a
19	    generic operator applied to a pair, and walk's generic methods that
20	    differ in their number of parameters.
